# ── Published papers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The PDFs in papers/ are copyrighted (Elsevier, Springer, IEEE). This repository is
# PUBLIC, so committing them would redistribute paywalled work. They are referenced by
# citation in docs/PIPELINE.md instead. Keep them locally; do not commit.
papers/*.pdf
papers/*.PDF

# ── Regenerable training data ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# 66 MB, and `src/build_groups.py --seed 42` reproduces it deterministically in ~4 min.
# A 200-line sample of each split is committed under data/groups/samples/ so the schema
# is visible without cloning 66 MB.
data/groups/group_examples_*.jsonl
# Same deal on the LBSN track (46 MB, ~10 min):
#   python src/build_groups.py --data-dir ./data/lbsn --dataset LBSN_NYC \
#          --out-dir ./data/lbsn/groups --no-resplit
data/lbsn/groups/group_examples_*.jsonl
data/llmgpr/groups_social*/group_examples_*.jsonl

# ── Check-in data: COMMITTED on purpose ────────────────────────────────────
# The five Foursquare files (train/val/test_NYC.csv, poi_metadata_NYC.csv, vocab.pkl) are
# tracked so this repo is self-contained and a collaborator can clone-and-run. They are
# already public at eyamhamdi03/finetunning-LLada-MoE-poi-recommendation, TSMC2014 is a
# freely available research dataset, and FSQ Open Source Places is Apache-2.0. 21 MB total.
#
# Still ignored: the PRE-REGULARISER embedding file. It has no radial hierarchy
# (D1 rho=+0.03, flat radii) and is the file earlier runs silently trained on. The correct
# one is tracked at data/kg/poi_hyperbolic_embs_NYC.npy.
data/poi_hyperbolic_embs.npy

# ── Gowalla raw dump (figshare 22126586, the yongliu.org / Liu CIKM'13 crawl) ─
# 1.7 GB, six files, md5-verified against figshare's manifest. Re-download with the
# curl loop documented in LLMGPR_GOWALLA.md; derived parquets live beside them.
data/gowalla_raw/

# ── Run artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# _code/ is the notebook's module-staging dir when not on Kaggle (CODE_STAGE falls back to
# ./_code); outputs/ holds logs, checkpoints and results json from a run.
_code/
outputs/

# ── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── OS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
